TYPES
Public      -   Gobal identifiers to communicate over Internet (managed by ICAAN)
Private     -   Used within LAN and allows internal communicattion w/o direct exposure to the internet
LoopBack    -   Used for internal testing of devices network protocols
APIPA       -   Fallback for when DHCP fails, but are conisdered private IPs


DATA FLOWS
Unicast     -   Single source to a single destination
Mulitcast   -   Data travels from single source to multiple (but intentional) destination devices
Broadcast   -   Data travels from a single source to all devices on a destination network


IP ADDRESS ASSIGNMENT

Components
    - IP Address
    - Subnet Mask
    - Default Gateway
    - Server Address

Static  -   Manually assigning an IP Address

OR

Dynamic -   Automatically (BOOTP, DHCP, APIPA, ZeroConf)
